# Ultralytics re-downloads yolo11n.pt into the working directory whenever a
# model is trained or run locally, so the stray root-level copy is build
# detritus and is ignored.
#
# The rule is anchored to the repository root on purpose. Unanchored, it also
# matched ai/yolo11n.pt, and the only reason that never bit was that the file
# was already tracked -- .gitignore has no effect on tracked paths. Any
# `git rm --cached ai/yolo11n.pt` (or a fresh clone that somehow lost it) would
# have left the ignore rule active, so the weight could not be re-added and the
# AI image would silently build without it.
#
# ai/yolo11n.pt is deliberately committed: it is the default person/vehicle
# detector weight that docker/ai/Dockerfile copies into the image, so a fresh
# clone runs real inference without reaching the network. See
# docs/adding-a-detector.md and docs/limitations.md. Keep it tracked.
/yolo11n.pt
!ai/yolo11n.pt

# Prisma migrations live in backend/prisma/migrations and MUST stay tracked, so
# there is deliberately no ignore rule for them here.
#
# Keep every `.env` ignore above this line and this negation directly below it.
# Git resolves patterns last-match-wins, so a broader `.env*` appended after
# this point silently shadows the negation and drops all four .env.example
# templates (root, ai/, backend/, frontend/) from a fresh clone.
!.env.example
